grep -i 'Status: Accepted'` inspects output with `grep` but asserts nothing — add an exit-code or comparison (-q, [ \"$(...)\" -eq N ], jq -e) so a failure is observable","verify command `grep -i 'mcp\\|blue-green' docs/adr/0079-autodeploy-on-box-timer.md` inspects output with `grep` but asserts nothing — add an exit-code or comparison (-q, [ \"$(...)\" -eq N ], jq -e) so a failure is observable","verify command `grep` inspects output with `grep` but asserts nothing — add an exit-code or comparison (-q, [ \"$(...)\" -eq N ], jq -e) so a failure is observable","verify command `grep` inspects output with `grep` but asserts nothing — add an exit-code or comparison (-q, [ \"$(...)\" -eq N ], jq -e) so a failure is observable"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add `auth_enabled = true` (and note `auth_strategies = static`) to the ADR's enumerated infra config keys so the static-verifier posture actually enforces auth, per mcp_server.py:600's build-verifier gate and :528's fail-closed unauthenticated-HTTP guard.","cohort":["T5c"],"criteria":["T5c"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.526,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan lists keys: 'transport, http_tls_at_edge, allowed hosts/origins, auth_resource_server_url, verifier static' — auth_enabled=true not among them","src/rebar/mcp_server.py:600 `auth_enabled = bool(mcp_cfg.auth_enabled)` gates building the composite verifier (lines 603-613)","src/rebar/mcp_server.py:528 `if not auth_enabled and not mcp_cfg.allow_unauthenticated_http:` — refuses to boot unauthenticated HTTP unless explicitly acknowledged","docs/mcp-auth.md §2 example pairs `auth_enabled = true` with `auth_strategies = static`"],"finding":"The ADR's enumerated infra config keys (transport, http_tls_at_edge, allowed hosts/origins, auth_resource_server_url, verifier static) omit the load-bearing auth-enforcement toggle auth_enabled=true. Per src/rebar/mcp_server.py:600-603 the composite token verifier is only built when auth_enabled is true; a static verifier + auth_resource_server_url with auth_enabled unset yields an unauthenticated HTTP surface, and mcp_server.py:528 shows non-loopback HTTP without auth refuses to boot unless allow_unauthenticated_http=true. On a public /mcp/ edge this is the difference between an authenticated bearer-gated server and an open one (OWASP A07 identification/authentication failure).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff609dfbca5c8e75b","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Decision 1 (exposure+auth) and AC line: 'The ADR names the concrete config keys the infra slice sets'","norm_id":"na763512c296e227a","priority":0.374,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Infra slice implements only the ADR-named keys, leaves auth_enabled at its default-off, and the box either refuses to boot or is forced to allow_unauthenticated_http, exposing an unauthenticated MCP server on the public /mcp/ edge"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"In Decision 1 and the config-keys AC, add `auth_enabled = true` and `auth_strategies = static` to the named keys, stating that auth_resource_server_url + verifier static are inert without auth_enabled=true (mcp_server.py:600-603).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.85,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_